2. **Color Patterns and Markings**: Wire-haired fox terriers typically have a white coat with patches of another color, most commonly black or gray. The patches can vary in size and shape, creating a unique and eye-catching pattern. Some dogs may also have a solid white coat.

3. **Size and Proportions**: The breed is relatively small, standing around 10-12 inches tall at the shoulder and weighing between 14-20 pounds. They have a compact body with a deep chest and a strong, muscular build.

